y":"acetaminophen_sched","drugClass":"Non-opioid analgesic / antipyretic","dose":"650 mg","route":"Oral","importantInfo":"Maximum 3 g per 24 hours from all sources. Check the temperature and pain score before giving.","monitoringRules":[{"label":"Temperature","sourceType":"vital","code":"TEMP"}],"highAlert":false,"freqKey":"daily","prn":false,"at":[],"hold":"","expires":"","barcode":"","expiredDecoy":false,"edited":false,"custom":false},"mar":{"category":"scheduled","orderStartIndex":0,"adminDose":"650 mg","dispenseLocation":"Pharmacy to load in ADS","completed":false,"lastAdmin":""}},{"id":"order_med_insulin_lispro_ssi_1","name":"insulin lispro (HUMALOG) injection","category":"Medication","status":"Active","frequency":"Daily","start":"2026-10-20 04:45","end":"","orderedAt":"2026-10-20 04:39","provider":"S. Patel, MD","instructions":"Check the blood glucose, then give insulin lispro SubQ by the LOW-DOSE sliding scale (glucose mg/dL: 150-199 = 2 units; 200-249 = 4 units; 250-299 = 6 units; 300-349 = 8 units; 350 or higher = 10 units and call the provider; below 150 = no insulin).","rationale":"Hyperglycemia (sliding-scale insulin)","linkedData":[],"nursingConsiderations":["Hold and notify the provider if glucose is below 70 mg/dL or the patient is not eating."],"medication":{"medKey":"insulin_lispro_ssi","drugClass":"Rapid-acting insulin","dose":"Per low-dose sliding scale","route":"Subcutaneous","importantInfo":"HIGH-ALERT. LOW-DOSE sliding scale (glucose mg/dL: 150-199 = 2 units; 200-249 = 4 units; 250-299 = 6 units; 300-349 = 8 units; 350 or higher = 10 units and call the provider; below 150 = no insulin). Check the glucose BEFORE giving, find the dose on the scale, and have a second nurse verify the dose per policy. Give within 15 minutes of a meal. Rotate sites (abdomen, thigh, upper arm). Watch for hypoglycemia: sweating, shakiness, confusion.","monitoringRules":[{"label":"Glucose","sourceType":"lab","code":"Glucose"}],"highAlert":true,"freqKey":"daily","prn":false,"at":[],"hold":"Hold and notify the provider if glucose is below 70 mg/dL or the patient is not eating.","expires":"","barcode":"","expiredDecoy":false,"edited":false,"custom":false},"mar":{"category":"scheduled","orderStartIndex":0,"adminDose":"Per low-dose sliding scale","dispenseLocation":"Pharmacy to load in ADS","completed":false,"lastAdmin":"","concentration":"100 units/mL"}},{"id":"order_med_ceftriaxone_im_2","name":"ceftriaxone (ROCEPHIN) injection","category":"Medication","status":"Active","frequency":"Daily","start":"2026-10-20 04:45","end":"","orderedAt":"2026-10-20 04:39","provider":"S. Patel, MD","instructions":"Administer 500 mg Intramuscular Daily.","rationale":"Bacterial infection","linkedData":[],"nursingConsiderations":[],"medication":{"medKey":"ceftriaxone_im","drugClass":"Cephalosporin antibiotic","dose":"500 mg","route":"Intramuscular","importantInfo":"Mixed with 1% lidocaine to reduce pain (500 mg per mL for this exercise): ask about lidocaine allergy. Deep IM in the ventrogluteal site; rotate sites; never more than 3 mL in one site. Verify the allergy list before every dose. Watch for rash and diarrhea.","monitoringRules":[{"label":"Temperature","sourceType":"vital","code":"TEMP"}],"highAlert":false,"freqKey":"daily","prn":false,"at":[],"hold":"","expires":"","barcode":"","expiredDecoy":false,"edited":false,"custom":false},"mar":{"category":"scheduled","orderStartIndex":0,"adminDose":"500 mg = 1 mL","dispenseLocation":"Pharmacy to load in ADS","completed":false,"lastAdmin":"","concentration":"500 mg/mL"}}],"administrations":[{"id":"admin_order_med_acetaminophen_sched_0_d0","orderId":"order_med_acetaminophen_sched_0","slotIndex":0,"time":"0900","state":"due","label":"0900 Due","dose":"650 mg","route":"Oral"},{"id":"admin_order_med_insulin_lispro_ssi_1_d0","orderId":"order_med_insulin_lispro_ssi_1","slotIndex":0,"time":"0900","state":"due","label":"0900 Due","dose":"Per low-dose sliding scale","route":"Subcutaneous"},{"id":"admin_order_med_ceftriaxone_im_2_d0","orderId":"order_med_ceftriaxone_im_2","slotIndex":0,"time":"0900","state":"due","label":"0900 Due","dose":"500 mg","route":"Intramuscular"}],"devices":[],"ioEvents":[],"stickyNotes":[{"title":"Medication pass","body":"Scan the patient wristband first, then scan each medication. Check the five rights and the hold parameters before giving."}],"notes":[{"id":"note_nursing_admission_note_2026_10_20_07_21","type":"progressNotes","title":"Nursing Admission Note","author":"T. Nguyen, RN","datetime":"2026-10-20 07:21","category":"Nursing Note","summary":"Admission database and baseline assessment completed.","body":"**Admission assessment**\n- Arrived to the unit at 0645 from the ED. ID band and allergy band verified (No known drug allergies.).\n- Vitals on arrival: T 99.7 F, HR 87, BP 122/75, RR 16, SpO2 98% on room air, pain 5/10.\n- General: Awake and alert, in no acute distress.\n- Cardiovascular: Normal sinus rhythm; S1 S2 regular, no murmur. Edema: None.\n- Respiratory: Clear bilaterally; unlabored, even.\n- Abdomen: Soft, non-tender, non-distended. Bowel sounds: active in all four quadrants.\n- Neurologic: Alert and oriented x4.\n- Skin: Right lateral hip: 10 x 8 cm bruise, tender, no open wounds.\n- Pain 5/10; right hip, aching, 5/10 with movement.\n- Skin: Right lateral hip: 10 x 8 cm bruise, tender, no open wounds. Braden 21.\n- Fall risk: High; fall precautions in place.\n- Lines: none.\n\n**Education**\n- Oriented to room, call light, plan of care, and fall precautions.\n\n**Plan**"},{"id":"note_hospitalist_history_and_physical_2026_10_20_07_15","type":"hp","title":"Hospitalist History and Physical","author":"S. Patel, MD","datetime":"2026-10-20 07:15","category":"H&P","summary":"Admission H&P for fall with urinary tract infection.","body":"**Chief complaint**\n- Fall at home and burning with urination\n\n**History of present illness**\n78-year-old female with type 2 diabetes who fell at home after 2 days of burning with urination and urgency. X-ray of the hip and pelvis shows no fracture; bruised right hip. Urinalysis positive for infection. Admitted for an intramuscular antibiotic, pain control and sliding-scale insulin.\n\n**Past medical history**\n- No significant past medical history.\n\n**Past surgical history**\n- No prior surgeries.\n\n**Home medications**\n- None\n\n**Allergies**\n- No known drug allergies.\n\n**Family history**\n- Mother with hypertension; father with coronary artery disease. No known family history of bowel disease or cancer.\n\n**Social history**\n- Lives with spouse/partner; independent with ADLs and ambulation at baseline; tobacco: never; alcohol: none; other substances: none.\n\n**Review of systems**\n- Positive for burning with urination, urgency, right hip pain and bruising. Negative for head strike, loss of consciousness, chest pain, shortness of breath, vomiting and flank pain.\n\n**Vitals**\n- T 99.7 F, HR 87, BP 122/75, RR 16, SpO2 98% on room air, pain 5/10 | Wt 64 kg, BMI 25.6\n\n**Physical exam**\n- General: Awake and alert, in no acute distress.\n- Cardiovascular: Normal sinus rhythm; S1 S2 regular, no murmur. Edema: None.\n- Respiratory: Clear bilaterally; unlabored, even.\n- Abdomen: Soft, non-tender, non-distended. Bowel sounds: active in all four quadrants.\n- Neurologic: Alert and oriented x4.\n- Skin: Right lateral hip: 10 x 8 cm bruise, tender, no open wounds.\n\n**Data**\n- Labs: \n\n**Assessment and plan**\n78-year-old female with no significant history admitted with fall with urinary tract infection.\n\n**Fall with urinary tract infection**\n\n**Prophylaxis / code status**\n- DVT prophylaxis per orders; fall precautions.\n- Code status: Full Code."},{"id":"note_ed_provider_note_2026_10_20_06_03","type":"erVisitSummary","title":"ED Provider Note","author":"J. Whitaker, MD","datetime":"2026-10-20 06:03","category":"ED Note","summary":"78-year-old female presenting with fall at home and burning with urination; admitted to Hospital Medicine.","body":"**Chief complaint**\n- Fall at home and burning with urination\n\n**HPI**\n78-year-old female with type 2 diabetes who fell at home after 2 days of burning with urination and urgency. X-ray of the hip and pelvis shows no fracture; bruised right hip. Urinalysis positive for infection. Admitted for an intramuscular antibiotic, pain control and sliding-scale insulin.\n\n**Past medical / surgical history**\n- Medical: No significant past medical history.\n- Surgical: No prior surgeries.\n\n**Allergies**\n- No known drug allergies.\n\n**Social history**\n- Lives with spouse/partner; independent with ADLs and ambulation at baseline; tobacco: never; alcohol: none; other substances: none.\n\n**Triage vitals**\n- T 99.6 F, HR 88, BP 123/73, RR 16, SpO2 98% on room air, pain 5/10\n\n**Exam**\n- General: Awake and alert, in no acute distress.\n- Cardiovascular: Normal sinus rhythm; S1 S2 regular, no murmur. Edema: None.\n- Respiratory: Clear bilaterally; unlabored, even.\n- Abdomen: Soft, non-tender, non-distended. Bowel sounds: active in all four quadrants.\n- Neurologic: Alert and oriented x4.\n- Skin: Right lateral hip: 10 x 8 cm bruise, tender, no open wounds.\n\n**ED results**\n- Labs: pending\n\n**ED course**\n- 0445 acetaminophen (TYLENOL) 650 mg Oral\n- 0445 insulin lispro (HUMALOG) Per low-dose sliding scale Subcutaneous\n- 0445 ceftriaxone (ROCEPHIN) 500 mg Intramuscular\n\n**Assessment / disposition**\n- Fall with urinary tract infection. \n- Admit to Hospital Medicine (Dr. S. Patel); condition guarded but stable."}],"timeline":{"marDate":"Tuesday, October 20, 2026","marTimeSlots":["0800","0900","1000","1100","1200","1300","1400","1500"],"simulationStart":"2026-10-20 08:45","simulationEnd":"2026-10-20 16:45"},"simulationTasks":[],"triggers":[],"facultyBuilder":{"builderVersion":2,"inputs":{"name":"Dorothy Hughes","age":78,"sex":"Female","mrn":"SIM-30413","unit":"Medical-Surgical 2 East","room":"208-1","heightCm":158,"weightKg":64,"primary":"lpn_fall","hospitalDay":1,"s